# Eleven survivors from one retry loop, all of them unobservable.
#
# `ring_poll` retries without parking. A budget of N means up to N attempts,
# with a `spin_loop` hint between them. Every test in this crate is
# single-threaded, and in a single thread nothing changes between attempts, so a
# repeated attempt can only find the answer the previous one found. That is the
# crate's own stated design, not a gap in the tests. Its doc says so directly:
# the budget "buys time for *another thread* to drain, not for this one to try
# harder."
#
# Nine of the eleven mutate a condition that guards nothing but the hint:
#
#     if attempt < budget.attempts()
#     {
#       core::hint::spin_loop();
#     }
#
# `spin_loop` is a hint to the CPU with no architectural effect. Whether it runs
# zero times or nine changes no value any caller can read, so no test can
# separate the mutants from the original. They are unkillable by construction,
# not by omission.
#
# The other two make the loop spend one extra attempt: `push_within` at 271 and
# `recv_within` at 387. The extra attempt is invisible for a reason specific to
# each: `try_push` hands the record back on refusal, and `try_recv` on an empty
# ring changes nothing at all. Both leave the state exactly as they found it, so
# attempt N+1 returns what attempt N returned.
#
# That reasoning is confirmed, not only asserted. Both were reinstated on
# 2026-08-30 and the suite stayed green, which is the same evidence the survey
# produced and the opposite of what the three fixed survivors produced.
#
# NOT accepted, and deliberately absent: 269, 273 and 277, all in
# `push_batch_within`, which looked identical to these and are not. One attempt
# there is a whole `try_push_batch`, which stops at its iterator's first `None`,
# and `Iterator` allows a `Some` after that `None`. So a source yielding one
# burst per attempt makes the attempt count observable in the published total.
# They are held by `mutant/S7`, `S8` and `S9`.

ring/ring_poll/src/lib.rs:298:17: replace < with <= in push_within
ring/ring_poll/src/lib.rs:307:20: replace < with <= in push_within
ring/ring_poll/src/lib.rs:307:20: replace < with == in push_within
ring/ring_poll/src/lib.rs:307:20: replace < with > in push_within
ring/ring_poll/src/lib.rs:378:16: replace < with <= in push_batch_within
ring/ring_poll/src/lib.rs:378:16: replace < with == in push_batch_within
ring/ring_poll/src/lib.rs:378:16: replace < with > in push_batch_within
ring/ring_poll/src/lib.rs:414:17: replace < with <= in recv_within
ring/ring_poll/src/lib.rs:421:16: replace < with <= in recv_within
ring/ring_poll/src/lib.rs:421:16: replace < with == in recv_within
